// Copy to Analytics.local.xcconfig and put the real token in it. That copy is
// git-ignored; this one is tracked, and it is how a clone learns the file is
// wanted. Without it the app builds, runs, and measures nothing.
//
// The token is the same value as POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN in .env. Both exist
// because an app opened from Finder inherits no shell: .env reaches
// `swift run`, and this reaches the bundle Xcode builds.
//
// Read it from the PostHog project, under Settings, Project, Project API key.
POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN = phc_your_project_token_here
